ChatBot AI
AI Chatbot for Software Engineers

An AI-powered chatbot built using the MERN stack and the OpenRouter API. It helps software engineers explore programming concepts, understand technical topics, and get assistance with software development questions.

Overview

ChatBot AI is a full-stack web application that combines an intuitive chat interface with large language models (LLMs) through the OpenRouter API.

The project demonstrates how to integrate an external AI service into a MERN stack application, manage frontend-backend communication, and create an interactive conversational experience tailored to developers.

Features
AI-Powered Conversations: Ask questions about programming, coding, and software development.
OpenRouter API Integration: Connect to supported large language models through OpenRouter.
Developer-Focused Assistance: Get explanations of programming concepts and help understanding technical problems.
Interactive Chat Interface: Communicate with the AI through a user-friendly conversational interface.
Full-Stack Architecture: Separate frontend and backend responsibilities for better organization and maintainability.
Secure API Integration: Route AI requests through the backend to keep API credentials out of the frontend.
Tech Stack
Frontend
React.js
JavaScript
HTML5
CSS3
Backend
Node.js
Express.js
AI Integration
OpenRouter API
Large Language Models (LLMs)
Database
MongoDB
How It Works
The user enters a programming question in the chatbot interface.
The React frontend sends the request to the backend server.
The Express.js server processes the request and forwards it to the OpenRouter API.
The selected language model generates a response.
The backend sends the response back to the frontend.
The chatbot displays the generated answer to the user.
Getting Started
Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following installed:

Node.js
npm (included with Node.js)
An OpenRouter API key
MongoDB, if required by your application
1. Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/Pooja9783/ai-chatbot.git
cd ai-chatbot

2. Install Dependencies

If your project has separate frontend and backend directories, install the dependencies for each.

Backend:

cd backend
npm install


Frontend:

Open a new terminal and run:

cd frontend
npm install


Note: Adjust the directory names according to your actual project structure.

3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a .env file in the backend directory and add the required environment variables.

PORT=5000
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key


If your application uses MongoDB, add your database connection string as well.

MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string


Replace the placeholder values with your actual configuration.

Security best practices:

Never commit your .env file or API keys to GitHub.
Add .env to your .gitignore file.
Keep API credentials on the backend and never expose them in frontend code.
4. Run the Application

Start the backend server from the backend directory using the appropriate script defined in its package.json. For example:

npm run dev


Then, open a separate terminal, navigate to the frontend directory, and start the frontend development server:

npm run dev


Open the local URL displayed in the frontend terminal to access the application.

Note: The commands may vary depending on the scripts configured in your package.json files.

OpenRouter API Integration

OpenRouter provides a unified API for accessing supported large language models. This project uses the OpenRouter API to send user prompts to a selected AI model and return generated responses to the chatbot interface.

The integration demonstrates:

Sending requests to an external AI service
Processing model-generated responses
Managing API communication through a backend server
Configuring API credentials using environment variables
Handling communication between the frontend and backend

Model availability, rate limits, and usage costs depend on the selected model and your OpenRouter account.

